#: ../pwntools/docs/source/args.rst:6
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.args` --- Magic Command-Line Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:1
msgid ""
"Pwntools exposes several magic command-line arguments and environment "
"variables when operating in `from pwn import *` mode."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:4
msgid ""
"The arguments extracted from the command-line and removed from "
"``sys.argv``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:6
msgid ""
"Arguments can be set by appending them to the command-line, or setting "
"them in the environment prefixed by ``PWNLIB_``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:9
msgid ""
"The easiest example is to enable more verbose debugging.  Just set "
"``DEBUG``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:16
msgid ""
"These arguments are automatically extracted, regardless of their name, "
"and exposed via :mod:`pwnlib.args.args`, which is exposed as the global "
"variable :data:`args`.  Arguments which ``pwntools`` reserves internally "
"are not exposed this way.  These reserved arguments (such as ``DEBUG`` "
"and ``NOASLR``) instead adjust :data:`pwnlib.context.context`, so their "
"effect is read from ``context`` (e.g. ``context.log_level``, "
"``context.aslr``) rather than from ``args`` -- ``args.NOASLR`` is always "
"the empty string."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:29
msgid ""
"This is very useful for conditional code, for example determining whether"
" to run an exploit locally or to connect to a remote server.  Arguments "
"which are not specified evaluate to an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:40
msgid "Arguments can also be accessed directly with the dot operator, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:47
msgid "Any undefined arguments evaluate to an empty string, ``''``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args:49
msgid ""
"The full list of supported \"magic arguments\" and their effects are "
"listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.args.PwnlibArgs.__weakref__:1
msgid "list of weak references to the object"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.DEBUG:1
msgid ""
"Sets the logging verbosity to ``debug`` which displays much more "
"information, including logging each byte sent by tubes."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.LOCAL_LIBCDB:1
msgid ""
"Sets path to local libc-database via ``context.local_libcdb``, e.g. "
"``LOCAL_LIBCDB='/path/to/libc-databse'``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.LOG_FILE:1
msgid ""
"Sets a log file to be used via ``context.log_file``, e.g. "
"``LOG_FILE=./log.txt``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.LOG_LEVEL:1
msgid ""
"Sets the logging verbosity used via ``context.log_level``, e.g. "
"``LOG_LEVEL=debug``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.NOASLR:1
msgid "Disables ASLR via ``context.aslr``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.NOPTRACE:1
msgid ""
"Disables facilities which require ``ptrace`` such as ``gdb.attach()`` "
"statements, via ``context.noptrace``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.NOTERM:1
msgid "Disables pretty terminal settings and animations."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.RANDOMIZE:1
msgid "Enables randomization of various pieces via ``context.randomize``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.SILENT:1
msgid "Sets the logging verbosity to ``error`` which silences most output."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.STDERR:1
msgid "Sends logging to ``stderr`` by default, instead of ``stdout``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.TIMEOUT:1
msgid ""
"Sets a timeout for tube operations (in seconds) via ``context.timeout``, "
"e.g. ``TIMEOUT=30``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.asbool:1
msgid "Convert a string to its boolean value"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.args.isident:1
msgid ""
"Helper function to check whether a string is a valid identifier, as "
"passed in on the command-line."
msgstr ""

